    "m_FunctionBody": "// frosted glass on 6.3: the camera's low-resolution copy (the low resolution IS most of the blur) sampled where this element\n// sits ON SCREEN (Rect* = the element's rect in panel-normalised units, y down), softened by a 5x5 tent, the theme tint on top\n// Element Layout UV runs bottom-up (measured: v 0 = the element's bottom), so FlipV 1 turns it into panel y-down first;\n// then panel y-down -> RenderTexture rows, which run bottom-up\nfloat layoutDownY = lerp(UV.y, 1.0 - UV.y, FlipV);\nfloat2 suv = float2(RectX + UV.x * RectW, RectY + layoutDownY * RectH);\nsuv.y = 1.0 - suv.y;\nfloat2 ts = Frost.texelSize.xy * Spread;\nfloat3 acc = 0;\nfloat wsum = 0;\nfor (int y = -2; y <= 2; y++)\n{\n    for (int x = -2; x <= 2; x++)\n    {\n        float w = (3 - abs(x)) * (3 - abs(y));\n        acc += SAMPLE_TEXTURE2D(Frost.tex, Frost.samplerstate, suv + float2(x, y) * ts).rgb * w;\n        wsum += w;\n    }\n}\nfloat3 frost = acc / wsum;\nColor = lerp(frost, float3(TintR, TintG, TintB), TintA);\nAlpha = 1.0;\n"
}

